.TH UNEGG 1 "2026-07-29" "unegg 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unegg \- extract files from an EGG archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unegg
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIARCHIVE\fR [\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
.B unegg
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fB\-\fR [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unegg
extracts files from an EGG archive, or lists its contents. With no \fIFILE\fR
operand every file is extracted; otherwise only the named \fIFILE\fRs are. A
single
.B \-
in place of \fIARCHIVE\fR reads the archive from standard input. Solid and split
(multi-volume) archives are handled transparently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List the archive contents; do not extract.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-output\-dir=\fIDIR\fR
Extract into \fIDIR\fR instead of the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pipe
Write extracted files to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password=\fIPW\fR
Decrypt the archive with password \fIPW\fR. When omitted, an encrypted archive
prompts on the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational messages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.PP
Short options may be bundled, for example
.BR \-lq .
An option that takes an argument accepts it joined or separate, and long options
accept it with
.RB ` = '
or as the next argument, so
.BR \-d DIR ", " "\-d " DIR ", " \-\-output\-dir=DIR ", and " "\-\-output\-dir " DIR
are equivalent.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred while reading or extracting the archive.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B unegg archive.egg
Extract every file into the current directory.
.TP
.B unegg \-d out/ \-P secret archive.egg
Extract an encrypted archive into \fBout/\fR.
.TP
.B unegg \-l archive.egg
List the archive contents.
